  bootwright / machine discover
      Record the disk identities of the selected powered-off physical machines: from the BMC
      drive inventory when it is complete, otherwise by booting inventory-only RHEL media and
      powering off. --name takes a comma-separated list. --dry-run previews without effects.
      --stage controller also plans controller and infrastructure setup; review the complete
      plan before confirmation. Discovery never installs an OS or creates RAID volumes.

  Usage
    bootwright machine discover [flags]

  Command flags
      --dry-run  Preview the discovery plan without booting a machine
      --name     Select comma-separated machine names (required)
      --stage    Select controller and infrastructure prerequisites for discovery (values:
                 controller)
      --yes      Confirm the command's ordinary confirmation

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  Examples
    bootwright machine discover --context lab --name node --stage controller --dry-run
